			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Brightly lit, standing solid against the gloom of the night, the academy that trained Felwithe’s paladins and clerics was bustling with an unnatural amount of activity. Like clockwork, pairs of students patrolled the halls, alert and watchful for an unknown enemy. It had been said that soon someone would strike at the heart of the school itself, and while no one was quite sure what that meant, they intended to stop whomever it was in their tracks. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp Two elves stood in the great hall, a centralized area for the patrols, watching the students through cool, glassy eyes. Both obviously paladins from their armor and weapons, they spoke quietly with each other, arms folded and nodding with approval as the next set checked in, reporting once again, there was nothing untoward, nothing of a clear and apparent danger. The younger of the two raised an eyebrow with a quirk of a grin and glanced up to his superior, “Same as ever, Jyleel.”
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
“Ah, yes,” the elder replied, “But that’s what we hope for, eh?”
<br />

<br />
 
<br />

<br />
 <i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
