			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Sitting on the Stairs the Samurai chuckles slightly before speaking ever so quietly more to himself then to the many who are around him... After having been gone so long the only thing that really can be said of him is... What happened to him, he has seemed to have retrieved some very interesting armor from the look of it. With some Strange eight pronged star etched into the breastplate. In other words it would have seemed the samurai has been away on another one of his quests to study the world of Norrath.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Who are we to say what is truth and what is a lie?&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He looks up Opalessent eyes glittering in the light, &quot;If truth were so easy to speak of, we wouldn't spend most of our lives fighting for a truth that we do not know of. But...&quot; He says as he stands up slowly bones creaking from lack of movement, his black and silvery scaled body tensing to relieve the strain of resting. &quot;A truth glimpsed, is a truth known. Fate, and destiny are fickle lovers. They will distort the truth my friends so one should be careful. Or... Lest ye be taken in their lovers dance and flung to the winds.&quot; He chuckles and smiles before bowing his head.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
